-- title:
--   Two mod-p readings of the Γ_H(M) chart ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$; assume `hj`, that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` $= q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for the full group. Write $\mathcal{O}_\Gamma$ for `chartAlgFin`, the subalgebra of elements of the level-$\Gamma$ $q$-expansion field integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $j$, for the two congruence subgroups `ΓM M H` and `ΓN p M H hpM`. Given an `R p`-algebra map $\iota_0 \colon \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_N} \to \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ preserving $q$-expansions, an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ with $\theta(\iota_0 b)(q) = b(q^p)$ (substitution `qExpand ℚ p`), a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed, and a ring map $\rho \colon$ `R p` $\to A$ lifting the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: there exist ring homomorphisms $\theta_0, \theta_1 \colon \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M} \to \kappa((q))$ with $\theta_1 = \theta_0 \circ \theta$; $\theta_0 c$ obtained by coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of any $y \in A((q))$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ is the $q$-expansion of $c$; $\ker \theta_0 \neq \ker \theta_1$; $\{\ker\theta_0, \ker\theta_1\}$ exactly the minimal primes of $p\,\mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$; $\theta_0(\theta(\iota_0 b)) = (\theta_0(\iota_0 b))^p = (\theta_0(\iota_0 b))(q^p)$ for all $b$; $\theta_0$ sending $c \in$ `R p` to the constant series with value the residue of $\rho(c)$; and all values of $\theta_0$ lying in the level-`ΓN p M H hpM` $q$-expansion field over $\kappa$.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the two-component structure of the mod-$p$ fibre of the modular curve $X_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$ (Deligne–Rapoport, Katz–Mazur): the two crossing branches correspond to the two minimal primes over $p$ of the $j$-finite chart ring, and the two readings differ by the Atkin–Lehner-type automorphism $\theta$, with Frobenius $q \mapsto q^p$ linking them on the lower-level subring. It feeds the construction of the pair of readings together with retractions, and its reduction to $\mathbb{Z}/n$ coefficients.
